@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Development Reflection";
}

<div class="container mt-5">
    <div class="card shadow-sm rounded-lg">
        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
            <h3 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-blog me-2"></i> My Activity Reflection</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
            <p>During this assignment, I gained practical experience building an ASP.NET Core MVC application. I learned</p>
            <p>how to move JavaScript to separate files for better organization, create reusable partial views like modals</p>
            <p>and filter forms, and enhance the UI with Bootstrap components such as tooltips, badges, and responsive</p>
            <p>tables. I also implemented dynamic features including modal interactions, toast notifications, and collapsible</p>
            <p>sections, as well as filter and reset functionality for better user experience. Overall, this project strengthened</p>
            <p>my understanding of MVC architecture, separation of concerns, and combining front-end and back-end</p>
            <p>development to create maintainable, interactive web applications. Moving forward, I plan to explore AJAX-</p>
            <p>based updates, client-side validation, and further UI improvements.</p>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>
